{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Two shoulders (אל שני)</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: \"as a sign that will come upon the two shoulders of your sons\" (Isaiah 9:5), \"and he placed upon the two shoulders of his young men\" (I Samuel 17:17), \"and he gave to the two youths, Naaman\" (II Kings 5:23). The sons of Eli despised the priesthood, about which is written אל שני; therefore they were punished and killed. But Naaman honored it, for he sought earth to make an altar, to draw near beneath the wings of the Shekhinah, and from his descendants Torah was taught in public."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:33.949685865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}